She was going to see her babies

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:39.350
- They should be hatching right about now.

00:23:39.350 --> 00:23:48.470
- Over there, baby box turtles.

00:23:48.470 --> 00:23:51.490
- So there are a few predators who can sometimes

00:23:51.490 --> 00:23:55.480
get past the amazing shell defense of the box turtle.

00:23:55.480 --> 00:24:00.000
Like coyotes, bears, raptors, fire ants.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.660
And the most dangerous of all, cars.

00:24:03.660 --> 00:24:09.080
But no doubt about it, the box turtle's defense is one of the best natural defenses in the

00:24:09.080 --> 00:24:12.310
entire creature world.

00:24:12.310 --> 00:24:17.370
The box turtle's shell is built to withstand incredible force.

00:24:17.370 --> 00:24:22.090
If you take a look at an old turtle shell like this one, this top part, that's called

00:24:22.090 --> 00:24:23.310
the carapace.

00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:30.000
You can see the turtle's spine is actually fused right into the top of the shell, and

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:36.100
All these bony plates and ribs in between them add structure to the shell.

00:24:36.100 --> 00:24:42.190
Now this bottom part, this is called the plastron, and it comes in two parts.

00:24:42.190 --> 00:24:46.580
This is the bottom part, and it fits right in here.

00:24:46.580 --> 00:24:52.640
And this part is hinged to it, so it can close whenever the turtle wants it to.

00:24:52.640 --> 00:24:54.420
And nothing can get inside.

00:24:54.420 --> 00:25:00.000
Now, there are lots of cool things about box turtles, besides that amazing

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:03.640
And one of those is watching a box turtle eat.

00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:06.040
- They eat all kinds of things.

00:25:06.040 --> 00:25:09.140
Worms, grass, mushrooms, and much more.

00:25:09.140 --> 00:25:11.100
And they really love fruit.

00:25:11.100 --> 00:25:13.020
- All kinds of fruit.

00:25:13.020 --> 00:25:15.590
And got some fruit for our buddy.

00:25:15.590 --> 00:25:18.550
- Now it's time for a Wild Kratz experiment.

00:25:18.550 --> 00:25:21.350
Let's see which fruit he likes best.

00:25:21.350 --> 00:25:23.870
- I think he's gonna go for that raspberry.

00:25:23.870 --> 00:25:26.070
- Oh, I am picking strawberry.

00:25:26.070 --> 00:25:27.980
- Look at that sharp beak.

00:25:27.980 --> 00:25:30.000
That can cut through fruit.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:33.710
Fruit and worms, it's kind of like a bird's beak.

00:25:33.710 --> 00:25:35.970
Go buddy, go, what do you like?

00:25:35.970 --> 00:25:40.120
Ooh, he's heading towards the watermelon.

00:25:40.120 --> 00:25:43.960
Wait a second, you're walking right by.

00:25:43.960 --> 00:25:45.220
No.

00:25:45.220 --> 00:25:46.410
Ooh.

00:25:46.410 --> 00:25:49.570
So that's what he was hungry for, a worm.

00:25:49.570 --> 00:25:53.020
Not all science experiments work out like you think.

00:25:53.020 --> 00:25:54.790
Enjoy.

00:25:54.790 --> 00:25:56.820
Keep on creature adventuring.

00:25:56.820 --> 00:25:58.610
We'll see you on the Creature Trail.

